godseyj@planetc.com wrote:
>Don't forget Sokoban, which I think made Nethack a large magnitude
>easier, with the guarantee'd wands and rings, not to mention the Prize.
>
>Generally I have found that there is a microscopically small chance of
>me getting to AC -18 without having obtained some form of reflection.

The issue is not with respect to the difficulty of finding a source of
reflection; it's with the fact that in 3.1.3, if you had a good enough
AC, you had no need for reflection.  This meant (remembering that 3.1.3
had neither twoweaponing nor SDSM and that player spells were basically
junk because of the way they worked) that a plausible AK could be built
which featured no source of reflection at all, allowing you to (for
example) wear an AoLS *and* use the Tsurugi.

Now, you *need* reflection if you intend to make safe use of rings and
wands in places where blue dragons or enemies with wands of lightning
are likely to appear.
